				<description>&lt;p&gt;In this post we will look into the the &lt;a href=&#34;https://leetcode.com/problems/min-cost-climbing-stairs/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;leetcode #746&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; problem to find the minimum cost of climbing stairs. This is also a good example to start your journey to learn dynamic programming.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem-statement&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Statement&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#problem-statement&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;You are given an integer array cost where &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cost[i]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; is the cost of &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ith&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; step on a staircase. Once you pay the cost, you can either climb one or two steps. You can either start from the step with index 0, or the step with index 1.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
